course: dictionary
lesson: 13364
title: Harshness in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Harshness is a noun, a word that names a quality. It means something is harsh: unkind, rough, or very hard to live in. You can work out its meaning from the words around it, such as «the harshness of the punishment» or «the harshness of winter».
explain: Harshness can describe people's behaviour. «The harshness of the teacher's words made Ben cry.» The clue is made Ben cry, so the words were cruel, not gentle. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then try your meaning in place of the hard word.
explain: Harshness can also describe things you see, hear or feel. «The harshness of the light hurt her eyes» means the light was glaring and unpleasant. «The harshness of the desert made travel very dangerous» means the place is extremely hard to live in.
fact: Harshness is a noun, so it names a quality, like kindness or sadness.
fact: «Harshness» can mean being unkind, strict or cruel, being rough and unpleasant to the senses, or being very difficult to live in.
fact: In a story, «the harshness of the punishment» means the punishment was strict or cruel.
fact: In geography and science, the harshness of a desert or the Arctic means the climate is extreme and hard to survive in.
fact: Animals in harsh places often have special adaptations, such as thick fur or ways to save water.
exercise: «The harshness of the punishment shocked the whole class.» What does harshness mean here? | Quietness | *Strictness and cruelty | Extreme heat | Kindness and fun
exercise: «The harshness of the Arctic winter means animals need thick fur.» What does harshness describe? | A loud noise | *The extreme, hard conditions of the climate | A friendly, gentle place | The colour of the snow
exercise: What kind of word is harshness? | A verb | *A noun | An adjective | A preposition
test: «The harshness of the light made Sam squint.» What does harshness mean in this sentence? | *Glaring and unpleasant to the senses | Gentle warmth | Being very far away | Soft and quiet
test: Which sentence uses harshness to mean being unkind? | *«The harshness of his reply hurt her feelings.» | «The harshness of the morning was bright and cheerful.» | «The harshness of the hill was covered in flowers.» | «The harshness of the sea was calm.»
exam: Harshness is a noun. In «The harshness of the desert made travel dangerous», what does it mean? | *Being extremely hard to live in | Being very bright | Being very quiet | Friendliness
